DevOps Interview Command Series — Kubernetes (Day 10) ☸️

Kubernetes is the backbone of container orchestration in modern DevOps.
From auto-scaling and self-healing to zero-downtime deployments, Kubernetes runs production at scale.

If you’re preparing for DevOps / SRE / Cloud interviews, these are the Kubernetes commands you must know:

kubectl version
kubectl cluster-info
kubectl get nodes
kubectl get namespaces

kubectl get pods
kubectl get pods -n namespace
kubectl describe pod pod-name
kubectl logs pod-name
kubectl logs pod-name -c container

kubectl exec -it pod-name -- /bin/sh
kubectl top pod
kubectl top node

kubectl apply -f file.yaml
kubectl delete -f file.yaml

kubectl get deploy
kubectl rollout status deploy app
kubectl rollout history deploy app
kubectl rollout undo deploy app

kubectl get svc
kubectl describe svc service-name
kubectl get ingress

kubectl get configmap
kubectl get secret

🎯 Interview Focus
• Pod lifecycle & crash troubleshooting
• Deployment strategies & rollbacks
• Service types & networking
• ConfigMaps vs Secrets
• Resource monitoring & scaling basics
• Kubernetes vs Docker runtime
